# iterative thinking — a coded rule asked ahead of the click turns the thinking to another try
#
# The wolf in the Test Den is an enemy in the same area, so UnderThreatImpossibleRule refuses any act
# that is not about facing it (unless the means is discreet). Without a retry the thinking would offer
# "examine the wolf" and the click would refuse it. With one (pineal_gland=1) the rules are asked while
# the thinking is still choosing (ActionRulesChecker.Probe): the refusal is shown in the means's voice,
# the mind tries again, and the act the click would refuse never becomes a button. The retry is the
# last one, so its own proposal is not probed — the click keeps the final word as it always had.
#
# Woodcraft is pinned as the first means (it observes, and is not discreet); the retry's pool has it
# crossed off, hence allow-flag-miss.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft --organs pineal_gland=1

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect wolf

strategy succeed
goal examine
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect while under the threat of
expect That will not do, and I think again
expect another way

allow-flag-miss --means-only
quit
